    "## Dataset: MovieLens 100K\n",
    "\n",
    "**Source:** GroupLens Research, University of Minnesota  \n",
    "**Version:** MovieLens 100K (`ml-100k`), a fixed benchmark released in April 1998. This is distinct from MovieLens “latest-small.”\n",
    "\n",
    "**Contents:** 100,000 ratings from 943 users on 1,682 movies. Ratings are whole numbers from 1 to 5, and each user has rated at least 20 movies. Data were collected between September 19, 1997, and April 22, 1998.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Access and download\n",
    "\n",
    "- Dataset page: https://grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/100k/\n",
    "- Direct ZIP download: https://files.grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/ml-100k.zip\n",
    "- Documentation and usage terms: https://files.grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/ml-100k-README.txt\n",
    "\n",
    "Download `ml-100k.zip` through a web browser and save it in the project’s `data/raw/` folder. Extract it there to create `data/raw/ml-100k/`. No account is required.\n",
    "\n",
    "For this project, a browser download was used because Python’s automatic download encountered an SSL certificate verification error.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Files used\n",
    "\n",
    "- `u.data`: Complete ratings dataset, with tab-separated fields: user ID, movie ID, rating, and Unix timestamp. The file has no header row.\n",
    "- `u.item`: Movie metadata, including titles and genres.\n",
    "- `u1.base` and `u1.test`: An official split containing 80,000 training ratings and 20,000 test ratings.\n",
    "- `README`: Dataset documentation and usage conditions.\n",
    "\n",
    "The notebook loads ratings from `data/raw/ml-100k/u.data`. Original files are retained in `data/raw/`; any cleaned exports are saved in `data/processed/`.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Usage and attribution\n",
    "\n",
    "The dataset is available for research under the conditions in its README. Publications must acknowledge its use. Redistribution and commercial or revenue-bearing use require separate permission from GroupLens.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Citation:** Harper, F. M., & Konstan, J. A. (2015). *The MovieLens Datasets: History and Context*. ACM Transactions on Interactive Intelligent Systems, 5(4), Article 19. https://doi.org/10.1145/2827872"
   ]
  },
